&lt;p&gt;Fueled is a leading digital strategy, design, and engineering agency. We are a 300+ person team that has designed and built hundreds of digital products and experiences for brands like Google, Apple, The New York Times, ESPN, Victoria’s Secret, MGM Resorts, Albertsons, and CLEAR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Product Designer&lt;/strong&gt; at Fueled, you will contribute to solving complex product challenges and shaping them into clear, high-value solutions, particularly within content-rich, CMS-driven environments. You will work closely with teammates and clients alike, helping shape experiences that ship, scale, and support structured content across digital products. This role is for a strong individual contributor who brings a thoughtful point of view, collaborative partnership, and attention to detail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Intentionally remote and globally distributed across six continents, our team thrives in a culture that values flexibility, creativity, and cutting-edge technology. Together, we’re shaping the future of digital experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design end-to-end experiences for content-rich, editorial, and information-heavy web and mobile products, often within CMS-driven and structured content environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and contribute to design systems and reusable patterns that support flexible content structures, ensuring scalability, consistency, polish, and long-term quality across projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with internal cross-discipline teams, contributing to solutions that align product, engineering, and strategy toward cohesive outcomes, while exploring innovative approaches and challenging assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support workshops and presentations as a key design contributor, building trust and credibility through clear storytelling, thoughtful communication, and demonstration of design impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use motion and interaction design strategically to enhance clarity, guide user attention, and reinforce experiences in ways that communicate intent and craftsmanship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will achieve:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver design experiences that users trust and teams can scale, turning insight into intuitive solutions across flows, screens, and interactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring clarity to complex, ambiguous challenges, helping teams and clients move forward with confidence and reduced friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen cross-functional alignment, contributing to shared understanding and measurable progress across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build client confidence through thoughtful design contributions, clear communication, and well-presented ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance the quality and consistency of design work across projects, using design systems, motion, and interaction to elevate outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About you:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3+ years of experience in visual, product, or digital design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in ambiguity, exploring complex challenges with curiosity and turning them into clear, value-driven product experiences, particularly within content-heavy or CMS-driven environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited by storytelling and strategy, articulating design decisions clearly and confidently to clients and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You collaborate effectively with cross-functional teams, contributing to alignment through thoughtful communication and shared problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring a high level of care and attention to detail to your work, with pride for design quality, visual craft, interaction, and motion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
